    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s12210-025-01368-8",
    "abstract": "Abstract This paper analyzes the seasonal and annual patterns of precipitation and temperature in the Castelporziano Nature Reserve from 1980. It also considers an index that combines precipitation and evapotranspiration. The results indicate various patterns within this small region, primarily influenced by the distance from the coast. Additionally, there is a clear upward trend in temperature. The joint analysis of precipitation and temperature shows that the most recent years have been characterized as either the hottest and driest or the hottest and most humid. Furthermore, there has been a significant increase in tropical nights and a longer duration of warm spells for maximum temperatures.",
    "field": "Regional climate change analysis",
    "problem": "Given the observed decline of ecosystems in the Castelporziano Presidential Estate, it is crucial to analyze local climate patterns and trends to understand the potential role of climate change as a primary driver of this degradation in a key Mediterranean conservation area.",
    "method": "This study analyzes climate patterns and trends by integrating meteorological station data with ERA5-Land reanalysis, applying trend tests, spatial interpolation, and standardized indices to assess changes in temperature, precipitation, and extreme events in the Castelporziano Nature Reserve.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze historical patterns and trends of temperature, precipitation, and extreme events in the Castelporziano Presidential Estate (Italy) using meteorological station and reanalysis data from 1980 onwards.",
    "model": [
        "ERA5-Land",
        "ERA5"
    ],
